<%# English translation of privacy-content.ejs. Keep it in sync with the Greek original (same variables and conditions). %>
  <p class="alert alert-info small translation-note">This is a translation provided for convenience. In case of any discrepancy, the Greek version prevails. <a href="<%= locals.siteUrl || '' %>/privacy" hreflang="el">Read the Greek version</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p><%= company.legalName %><% if (company.vat) { %>, VAT No. <%= company.vat %><% } %><% if (company.gemi) { %>, General Commercial Registry (GEMI) No. <%= company.gemi %><% } %><% if (company.seat) { %>, <%= company.seat %><% } %>.
    For personal data matters: <% if (company.privacyEmail) { %><a href="mailto:<%= company.privacyEmail %>"><%= company.privacyEmail %></a><% } else { %>via our <a href="<%= u('/contact') %>">contact form</a><% } %>.</p>

  <h2>2. What data we process, why and for how long</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="table">
    <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th><th>Retention period</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Booking and performance of the rental contract</td><td>Full name, email, telephone, date of birth, driving licence details, flight, notes, child’s details for a child seat, address for delivery/collection of the car (e.g. hotel)</td><td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>Driving licence details, date of birth, telephone, flight, notes, delivery/collection address: <%= config.retention.operationalMonths %> months after the return, unless a damage claim or a traffic penalty notice is pending</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tax documents (myDATA) and accounting records</td><td>Full name/company name, VAT No. (for an invoice), amounts, dates</td><td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</td><td>For as long as tax legislation requires</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Identifying the driver to the authorities for traffic offences committed during the rental</td><td>Driver and booking details</td><td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</td><td>Until the offence has been dealt with</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Security deposit, damage, fraud prevention, evidence in payment disputes</td><td>Card type and last 4 digits, authorisation code, vehicle condition reports and photographs of the car, correspondence</td><td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)): protecting our fleet and defending legal claims</td><td>Until the security deposit is settled and the related claims become time-barred</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customer account</td><td>Email, password (encrypted), name, telephone</td><td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>Until the account is deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Replying to messages and complaints</td><td>Name, email, telephone, message</td><td>Legitimate interest / pre-contractual measures</td><td><%= config.retention.messagesMonths %> months</td></tr>
      <% if (company.whatsapp) { %><tr><td>Contact via WhatsApp (optional)</td><td>Telephone number, WhatsApp profile name, content of the messages</td><td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) for messages about your booking; for other questions, legitimate interest / pre-contractual measures</td><td><%= config.retention.messagesMonths %> months (we delete older chats)</td></tr><% } %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>Providing the booking details is necessary for concluding the contract; without them we cannot complete the booking. The checks on the driver’s age and how long they have held a driving licence are carried out automatically, based on the published rules; you can contact us to have the decision reviewed by a member of our staff. We do not send marketing messages without your consent.</p>
  <% if (company.whatsapp) { %><p id="whatsapp"><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> contacting us via WhatsApp is optional and is your choice; you can always call us, email us or use the contact form. If you write to us on WhatsApp, we see your telephone number, your profile name and whatever you send us. We may also send you a short message about your booking on WhatsApp, to the telephone number you gave in the booking (e.g. that the car is ready, or to ask for your flight number); if you do not want this, tell us and we will contact you another way. The WhatsApp service is provided by WhatsApp Ireland Limited (Meta group), which processes the data relating to the use of the service in accordance with its own terms and privacy policy. We do not use WhatsApp for marketing messages.</p><% } %>

  <h2>3. Card details</h2>
  <p>Card payments are made on the secure page of the payment provider (Stripe or Revolut) or on our bank’s POS terminal. <strong>We do not see or store the full number or the CVV of your card.</strong> For the security deposit we store only the card type (e.g. Visa credit), the last 4 digits and the authorisation code.</p>

  <h2>4. Recipients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Payment providers: Stripe Payments Europe Ltd. and/or Revolut, and the bank that operates our POS terminal. The payment providers also act as independent controllers for their own obligations (e.g. fraud prevention).</li>
    <li>Website hosting and email delivery providers (processors, under a contract pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR).</li>
    <li>Our accountant and e-invoicing provider, and the Independent Authority for Public Revenue (AADE) (myDATA).</li>
    <li>The insurance company (in the event of damage or an accident), and the authorities (Traffic Police, municipalities) where required by law.</li>
    <% if (company.whatsapp) { %><li>WhatsApp Ireland Limited (Meta group), only if we communicate via WhatsApp.</li><% } %>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Transfers outside the EEA</h2>
  <p>Some providers (e.g. the Stripe group<% if (company.whatsapp) { %> and the Meta group for WhatsApp<% } %>) may process data in the United States. Such transfers take place on the basis of the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and data portability. You can download your data or delete your account from the ‘My account’ page, or write to us; we reply within one month. On deletion, we keep only what tax legislation requires or what relates to a pending claim.</p>
  <p><strong>Right to object (Article 21 GDPR):</strong> you may object at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to processing based on our legitimate interest.</p>
  <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (www.dpa.gr).</p>
  <p>Additional drivers are informed about the processing of their data by means of a printed notice at pick-up.</p>

  <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use <strong>only one strictly necessary cookie</strong>, <code>sid</code>, for logging in to your account, keeping forms secure and completing your booking. It lasts until you close your browser (or 30 days, if you select ‘Remember me’ when logging in). We do not use advertising or analytics cookies, so no consent is required.</p>
